spans.s:
अति-क्रम, अस्, m. act of passing or overstepping;
lapse (of time); overcoming, surpassing, conquering;
excess, imposition, transgression, violation; neglect;
determined onset.

अति-ग्रह, अस्, m. act of overtaking or surpassing;
one who takes or seizes to an extraordinary extent;
(in philosophy) the same as अतिग्राह.

अति-देश, अस्, m. transfer, extended application,
inference, analogy, overruling influence, assimilation;
a rule providing for more than the usual rule; putting
one thing instead of another, substitution; रूपाति-
देश, such a rule as affecting the form of a word;
(अस्, आ, अम्,), overruling, previously stated.

अति-पत्ति, इस्, f. going beyond, passing, lapse;
क्रियातिपत्ति, the passing by of an action unaccom-
plished.

अतिशी अति-शी, cl. 2. A. -शेते, -शयितुम्, to
precede in lying down; to surpass, excel, exceed;
to act as an incubus, annoy.

आतिथेय आतिथेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अतिथि, q. v.),
proper for a guest, hospitable, attentive to a guest;
(ई or अम्), f. n. hospitality.
